        "original_id": "e27b7835-78c5-55bf-b8a3-26dbb0ab5daf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Elmer Clifton, D. W. Griffith, Joseph Henabery, Paige Lewis, Eric Garcia\n- Films: Alien, Blade Runner, Gladiator, The Martian, The Birth of a Nation, Intolerance, Matchstick Men\n- Roles: film director, producer, actor, mentor, singer-songwriter, copywriter\n- Places: England, Katy, Texas\n\nFacts:\n- Ridley Scott was born on 30 November 1937 and is an English film director and producer.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in The Birth of a Nation in 1915 as a collaborator of D. W. Griffith.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in Intolerance in 1916.\n- Elmer Clifton gave up acting in 1917 to concentrate on behind-the-camera work, with D. W. Griffith and Joseph Henabery as his mentors.\n- Ridley Scott had a commercial breakthrough with Alien in 1979.\n- Ridley Scott directed Blade Runner in 1982.\n- Matchstick Men is a 2003 British-American black comedy crime film directed by Ridley Scott and based on Eric Garcia's 2002 novel of the same name.\n- Gladiator, directed by Ridley Scott, won the Best Picture Oscar in 2000.\n- Paige Lewis is a singer-songwriter and copywriter from Katy, Texas.\n- Paige Lewis's work was featured in the soundtrack of Matchstick Men.\n- Ridley Scott directed The Martian in 2015.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
